SUMMARY:The Beautiful Game: A Playable History of Soccer Video Games
LOCATION:Royal Ontario Museum\, 100 Queen's Park
DESCRIPTION:The Beautiful Game presents a playable selection of soccer vide
 o games spanning the last 50 years. The exhibit traces how the world’s m
 ost popular sport has been imagined for players on screen. It invites visi
 tors to celebrate soccer’s global history through play as the beautiful 
 game comes home to Toronto.\nDates/times: Thursday\, June 11: 11am-4pm\nFr
 iday\, June 12: 11am-4pm\nSaturday\, June 13: 11am-4pm\nSunday\, June 14: 
 11am-4pm\nMONDAY – ROM CLOSED\nTuesday\, June 16: 11am-8pm (free general
  admission starting at 4pm)\nWednesday\, June 17: 11am-4pm\nRegistration: 
 Tickets required.\nLink: https://tickets.rom.on.ca/en/shop\nMap: 100 Queen
 's Park
URL:https://tickets.rom.on.ca/en/shop
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6633b8ae6ac1051b79668d5d0a16ddda49ee399f@torontogamesweek.com
DTSTAMP:20261127T033536Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T190000
SUMMARY:Journalling for Your Games and Creative Work
LOCATION:Fort York Public Library\, 190 Fort York Blvd.
DESCRIPTION:There are many challenges to bring a project to life\, includin
 g in technical\, creative\, and business processes. Join Tanya Kan from th
 e game studio Vivid Foundry in a journalling workshop to reflect on your g
 oals and priorities. Whether you’re working on a 1-month art piece or a 
 4-year game\, let’s be motivated in our human-first creative journey!\nD
 ates/times: I would like to request 2 hours if possible\, though 1.5 hours
  minimum can still work! Plus\, a 30 min networking space after the sessio
 n will be grand. I think the latter is even more important.\nPrice: PWYC.\
 nRegistration: Registration required.\nLink: https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/j
 ournalling-for-your-games-and-creative-work-tickets-1989288265753\nMap: 19
 0 Fort York Blvd
URL:https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/journalling-for-your-games-and-creative-wor
 k-tickets-1989288265753
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:87db1eaa4be639da9bf8cf4bbe6a68f2f5092b8a@torontogamesweek.com
DTSTAMP:20261127T033536Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T200000
SUMMARY:An Intro to DaggerHeart
LOCATION:Port Union Public Library\, 5450 Lawrence Ave. E.
DESCRIPTION:Come learn the ins and outs of the tabletop roleplaying phenome
 non known as DaggerHeart. Players will fall into the roles of our heroic a
 dventurers and prove they have the strength\, skills\, knowledge and brave
 ry to become the Games Week Champions! No prior TTRPG experience required.
 \nPrice: Free!\nRegistration: Registration required.\nLink: https://tpl.bi
 bliocommons.com/v2/events/69d6a557c1cf6f9a758407d0\nMap: 5450 Lawrence Ave
  E
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d6a557c1cf6f9a758407d0
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2bc60b84f2f8d63bf23919e0d2845a86c1d68e7d@torontogamesweek.com
DTSTAMP:20261127T033536Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T200000
SUMMARY:Secrets of MUDs and MUSHes from a Werewolf Elder
LOCATION:Fort York Public Library\, 190 Fort York Blvd.
DESCRIPTION:Come learn about the history of MUDs and MUSHes from a longtime
  RetroMUX community Storyteller! Find out how the very first online rolepl
 aying games persist after more than 45 years\, plus\, come play (bring a l
 aptop\, tablet\, or phone!) on a noob-friendly MUSH set in cyberpunk Toron
 to specially designed for TGW.\nPrice: Free\, just show up!\nMap: 190 Fort
  York Blvd
END:VEVENT
