BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cb528a1103b93582f9d7c9650afb3ee6841b7d56@torontogamesweek.com
DTSTAMP:20261127T033536Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T210000
SUMMARY:Hand Eye Society x Luminato at Sankofa Square
LOCATION:Sankofa Square\, 1 Dundas St E.
DESCRIPTION:As part of Luminato at Sankofa Square\, Hand Eye Society will p
 resent the Torontron arcade cabinets featuring indie games by local develo
 pers and game artists. The event invites indie game devs to meet up and ex
 perience newly created video games\, alongside special performances by Lum
 inato artists. Games\, circuses\, and concerts\, oh my!\nPrice: Free\, jus
 t show up!\nRegistration: More info here.\nLink: https://www.luminatofesti
 val.com/luminato-at-sankofa-square\nMap: 1 Dundas St E
URL:https://www.luminatofestival.com/luminato-at-sankofa-square
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:71968a160f6652d9d191cd0d427c0419fb5043cc@torontogamesweek.com
DTSTAMP:20261127T033536Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T210000
SUMMARY:The G.R.I.D.
LOCATION:George Brown Polytechnic WaterFront Campus\, 3 Lower Jarvis St.
DESCRIPTION:The G.R.I.D. is a welcoming\, behind-the-scenes space where ind
 ie devs\, studios\, and solo creators can show off their games\, get hones
 t\, helpful feedback\, and keep improving - no matter what stage the game
 ’s in. It’s all about structure\, support\, and moving your project fo
 rward with fresh eyes and solid input. Registration required for playteste
 rs or developers.\nPrice: Free!\nRegistration: Registration required.\nLin
 k: https://playthegrid.games\nMap: 3 Lower Jarvis St
URL:https://playthegrid.games
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e6aa5244b243817e81763e259fc79b5a29692458@torontogamesweek.com
DTSTAMP:20261127T033536Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T203000
SUMMARY:No Bosses! Real talk from Toronto's cooperative game studios
LOCATION:North York Central Auditorium\, 5120 Yonge St.
DESCRIPTION:Meet Toronto indie game studios building a different kind of in
 dustry -- one rooted in workers' rights\, sustainability\, and cooperation
 . In this roundtable\, studio members share what they're learning as they 
 build cooperative game studios from the ground up. Stick around to mingle 
 after.\nPrice: Free!\nRegistration: Registration required.\nLink: https://
 babyghosts.fund/events/no-bosses\nMap: 5120 Yonge St
URL:https://babyghosts.fund/events/no-bosses
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:db74df116b26fa66c67a892a243496d88eb998b3@torontogamesweek.com
DTSTAMP:20261127T033536Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T200000
SUMMARY:The Sounds That Shape Play: A Toronto Game Audio Roundtable
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith Public Library\, 239 College St\, lower level
DESCRIPTION:Hosted by the Toronto Game Audio Collective (TGAC)\, this inter
 active roundtable session will bring together game audio creatives from ac
 ross the GTA to connect to\, learn from\, and inspire one another. At this
  roundtable\, we will explore how composers and audio artists can lead a g
 ame’s creative direction through sound. This session is open to all prof
 essional\, aspiring and enthusiasts of video game audio!\nPrice: Free!\nRe
 gistration: FULL\, waitlist here.\nLink: https://torontogameaudioroundtabl
 e.eventbrite.com\nMap: 239 College St
URL:https://torontogameaudioroundtable.eventbrite.com
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ce142773a942afe3ad1f3c5d6d71caf410d60d82@torontogamesweek.com
DTSTAMP:20261127T033536Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T203000
SUMMARY:Stoppage Time: A Despelote Live Play With Creator Julián Cordero
LOCATION:U of T Bahen Centre\, 40 St. George St.\, 1160 Adel Sedra Auditori
 um
DESCRIPTION:IGF winner and Game Awards nom Despelote explores 2001 Ecuador\
 , as the community is captivated by high stakes soccer. An autobiographica
 l game\, you play as eight year old Julián Cordero\, witnessing a world l
 ocked in anticipation. FUNLAND Zine proudly welcomes Cordero to an intimat
 e\, in-person live play of the game\, where he will give insights into its
  creation.\nPrice: Free\, just show up!\nMap: 40 St George St
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0f56b26af2e929902739e6964a6ece4019e2987f@torontogamesweek.com
DTSTAMP:20261127T033536Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T230000
SUMMARY:Get Social @ FreePlay
LOCATION:FreePlay Toronto Retro Arcade Bar\, 300 College St.
DESCRIPTION:End the night playing games and sipping bevvies with fellow TGW
  attendees at this local arcade bar! Trade stories and maybe go head to he
 ad with new pals. All are welcome! Entry fee includes unlimited games and 
 pinball machines.\nPrice: $10\nRegistration: Cover at the door.\nMap: 300 
 College St
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:04a9873b7cf66b93912a0bb7f32467fc520e247d@torontogamesweek.com
DTSTAMP:20261127T033536Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T204500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T235900
SUMMARY:Toronto Escape Room Meetup and Many Happy Returns Kick-off Party
LOCATION:Casa Loma\, 1 Austin Terrace
DESCRIPTION:Every month\, the Toronto Escape Room Meetup hits up an escape 
 room followed by a hangout at a nearby pub. This month\, join us as we do 
 a one-hour escape room and then go to a pub to celebrate the kickoff of ou
 r organizer’s immersive show (Many Happy Returns) coming to Toronto Frin
 ge 2026! Join the Meetup group to register\, pre-pay\, and for pub timing.
 \nDates/times: Escape rooms will be 1 hour each and start around 8\; we wi
 ll then go to the afterparty location at a pub in the Annex (TBD) and be t
 here until the crowd dissipates or the venue closes for the night.\nPrice:
  $60\nRegistration: Registration required.\nLink: https://www.meetup.com/t
 oronto-escape-rooms/\nMap: 1 Austin Terrace
URL:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-escape-rooms/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1d6f8a5e95aa2959121e81768961602eccb5969d@torontogamesweek.com
DTSTAMP:20261127T033536Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T160000
SUMMARY:Open World Map: Digital Sovereignty for Game Creators
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith Public Library\, 239 College St.
DESCRIPTION:Enshittified platforms and proprietary tools are not only makin
 g the world worse\, but they make it harder for game creators to connect w
 ith an audience. But as tech-savvy systems thinkers\, game creators are un
 iquely positioned to push back in a number of ways. Join us for an inspiri
 ng day of discussion\, demos\, and workshops featuring: open source game d
 ev tool alternatives from Matt Hammill (Lovers in a Dangerous Spacetime)\,
  Mastodon tips and tricks from Rob Gehl (Move Slowly and Build Bridges fro
 m Oxford Press)\, playing with open protocols with Christine Lemmer-Webber
  and David Thompson (ActivityPub and Spritely Foundation)\, and liberating
  D&D data with Cousin Vagabond!\nPrice: Free!\nRegistration: Registration 
 required.\nLink: https://luma.com/8nvmyatm\nMap: 239 College St
URL:https://luma.com/8nvmyatm
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5bfcc44443dd4ac60044e80ede55038c94b6b9fd@torontogamesweek.com
DTSTAMP:20261127T033536Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T120000
SUMMARY:Gym Game Gauntlet
LOCATION:Riverdale Park East\, 550 Broadview Ave.
DESCRIPTION:Think Mario Party\, but with classic gym class games from child
 hood! Outdoor favourites like Fishes and Minnows\, Duck Duck Goose\, Freez
 e Tag\, and more! All this and a six-foot high soccer ball in play\, too!\
 nPrice: Free\, just show up!\nMap: 550 Broadview Ave
END:VEVENT
