UID:89cce70f072925bae3f56e53e8c613c982e98ada@torontogamesweek.com
DTSTAMP:20261127T033536Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T213000
SUMMARY:Hand Eye Society x Luminato at Harbourfront
LOCATION:Harbourfront\, 235 Queens Quay W.
DESCRIPTION:Hand Eye Society brings Torontron arcade cabinets to Luminato a
 t Harbourfront\, featuring indie games by local developers and game artist
 s. Blending arcade play with local game art\, the installation offers fest
 ival-goers a fun and accessible way to experience video games as art.\nPri
 ce: Free\, just show up!\nMap: 235 Queens Quay West
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:847ca0804c78bcdfed27f917aa7b8b048ee18320@torontogamesweek.com
DTSTAMP:20261127T033536Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T140000
SUMMARY:nonsensitive workshop
LOCATION:U of T Bahen Centre\, 40 St. George St.
DESCRIPTION:In this cognitive imagination workshop\, literally and figurati
 vely map your internal world\, crafting abstracted artifacts generated thr
 ough a poetic reimagining of psychological profiling and journaling keepsa
 ke games. Materials provided\, though you may bring your own journal or sk
 etchbook. Part of the <a href="https://dmgregory.ca/tgw/">“Play Outside 
 the Box”</a> event series.\nPrice: Free!\nRegistration: Registration req
 uired.\nLink: https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/nonsensitive-workshop-tickets-19
 87182082101\nMap: 40 St George St
URL:https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/nonsensitive-workshop-tickets-1987182082101
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:205728d273154a7f43efaf0c081d049ae9b9eda4@torontogamesweek.com
DTSTAMP:20261127T033536Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T180000
SUMMARY:Pokémon Proxy Party
LOCATION:Mad Merchant Cards and Games\, Splendid China Mall - 4675 Steeles 
 Ave. E Unit 1D20\, 1D22\, & 1D25
DESCRIPTION:A laid-back art anthology for Pokémon fans and creators. In ju
 st two hours\, you’ll contribute to a massive\, community-built collecti
 on of the original 151 custom proxy designs. No pressure to be perfect. Th
 e $20 fee includes a drink\, art supplies\, and a custom card.\nDates/time
 s: We will be having multiple six different 2 hour sessions:\n\nSat June 1
 3th @ 12pm - 2pm\nSat June 13 @ 2pm - 4pm \nSat June 13 @ 4pm - 6pm \nSun 
 June 14 @ 12pm - 2pm \nSun June 14 @ 2pm - 4pm\nSun June 14 @ 2pm - 6pm\nP
 rice: $20\nRegistration: Registration required.\nLink: https://www.eventbr
 ite.com/e/pokemon-proxy-party-tickets-1989100554303?aff=oddtdtcreator\nMap
 : 4675 Steeles Ave E
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/pokemon-proxy-party-tickets-1989100554303?
 aff=oddtdtcreator
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:81d44f5ebac112f0363846243e637f7fc938a105@torontogamesweek.com
DTSTAMP:20261127T033536Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T180000
SUMMARY:CTRL-ALT-DELICIOUS
LOCATION:U of T Bahen Centre\, 40 St. George St.
DESCRIPTION:A playful exhibition of alternative control games: ones that do
  something unconventional at the interface between players\, audience\, an
 d game system (think custom controllers or games you play with your body).
  Stop by and play some games you won't find online! Part of the <a href="h
 ttps://dmgregory.ca/tgw/">“Play Outside the Box”</a> event series.\nPr
 ice: Free!\nRegistration: More info here.\nLink: https://dmgregory.ca/tgw/
 \nMap: 40 St George St
URL:https://dmgregory.ca/tgw/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e907e8916c7cd74ee0428fa1eb1fa18ed5d5490c@torontogamesweek.com
DTSTAMP:20261127T033536Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T170000
SUMMARY:Kick-Off & Play: Soccer Board Game Fest
LOCATION:Twilight Cafe & Bar (North York)\, 16 Park Home Ave.
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a free soccer-themed board game event! Enjoy games 
 like Counter Attack\, Superclub and UND1C1. Whether you're a hardcore stra
 tegist or just curious\, there’s something for everyone. Just show up\, 
 learn new games\, and connect with fellow soccer and board game fans in a 
 fun\, relaxed setting.\nDates/times: NA\nPrice: Free!\nRegistration: Regis
 tration required.\nLink: https://www.meetup.com/board-games-social/events/
 314232234/\nMap: 16 Park Home Ave
URL:https://www.meetup.com/board-games-social/events/314232234/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4b0705e23d521dd338da051c72dcde6b17f0b9f9@torontogamesweek.com
DTSTAMP:20261127T033536Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T160000
SUMMARY:Fight and Ye Shall Receive: How Game Worker Unions Win!
LOCATION:TacoTaco\, 319 Augusta Ave.
DESCRIPTION:Game workers from across the continent will discuss the histori
 c rise of the game industry labour movement\, how unions are making change
 s in our industry\, and visions for the future! If you've  wondered how un
 ionization could change your workplace and our whole industry\, this talk 
 is for you! A Q&A session and mixer with snacks will follow!\nPrice: Free!
 \nRegistration: Registration required.\nLink: https://actionnetwork.org/ev
 ents/ask-and-ye-shall-receive-how-game-worker-union-campaigns-are-chaning-
 the-industry?source=direct_link&\nMap: 319 Augusta Ave
URL:https://actionnetwork.org/events/ask-and-ye-shall-receive-how-game-work
 er-union-campaigns-are-chaning-the-industry?source=direct_link&
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:989ee920de10aeb991318a8c6726e1cfbf53b1d5@torontogamesweek.com
DTSTAMP:20261127T033536Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T153000
SUMMARY:Vector Festival Gamemaking Residency: Open Studios
LOCATION:InterAccess\, 32 Lisgar St.
DESCRIPTION:Join our Gamemakers-in-Residence for a peek into their in-progr
 ess\, experimental video games\, created as part of "Where are your guts?"
 \, the Vector Festival Gamemaking Residency\, curated by Bracy Appeikumoh.
  Games are focused on cyborg-forward game mechanics\, symbiotic systems\, 
 and reconciliations between bodies and bots.  Also: Do you want to be a co
 g in your own machine? Join artist Tristan Sauer for a mixed-media generat
 ive performance exploring how digital layers of LLMs\, digital avatars\, a
 nd digital communication devices abstract\, co-opt\, and reinterpret human
  communication.\nPrice: Free!\nRegistration: Registration requested\nLink:
  https://www.interaccess.org/vector-festival/vf26/vf26-gamemaking-residenc
 y-application\nMap: 32 Lisgar St
URL:https://www.interaccess.org/vector-festival/vf26/vf26-gamemaking-reside
 ncy-application
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
